 "transcript": [
  "[action] (to the eldest son, the second son) Wang Lung listens and asks his sons.",
  "Wang Lung (to the eldest son, the second son): \"Tell your old father what I have heard you are always talking about and what business you have in the town.\"",
  "the eldest son (to the second son): \"Well, and what business have we in the town? Why, father, there is a great grain market and a great storehouse in the town, and we are selling grain and buying grain and selling grain and buying grain again and so on and so on until we are rich as the great men of the town and we shall live in great houses and have many servants and we shall be great men and be looked upon as men like the rich men of the town.\"",
  "[action] (to the eldest son, the second son) The sons talk to Wang Lung about their wealth.",
  "Wang Lung (to the eldest son, the second son): \"I do not know what you mean!\"",
  "[action] (to Wang Lung) The eldest son is proud of his wealth.",
  "[action] puffs up his chest",
  "the eldest son (to Wang Lung): \"And we are selling grain and buying grain and selling again and again until we are rich as the rich men of the town and live in great houses with many servants and we shall be great men like the rich men of the town.\"",
  "[action] Wang Lung sits and smokes his pipe, listening.",
